  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nA weak s/w passing through srn CWA Wed afternoon will combine with\ndaytime heating to bring a chance of showers to the se half of the\nCWA into Wed evening. S/w energy ahead of the next upper trough will\npush east and into the CWA Thurs night, bringing the next chance of\nactivity. The trough broadens as its parent circulation tracks\nnortheast on Friday, but lingers over the region through about\nSunday. This scenario makes it necessary to keep some shower activity\nin the CWA during this time. \n\nGiven the expected increase in cloud cover during the day and\nincreased moisture overnight, highs are progged to be near normal,\nand lows above normal through the forecast period.",
